  "clockRules": {
    "origin": "One immutable coordinator monotonic t0 before initial fresh root-envelope validation. Denial admits no child; if authorized, every authentication/setup/tool/guard/control/wait/capture/type/mutation/cleanup interval stays under this same origin.",
    "globalDeadline": "t0 + globalMonotonicCapMs; never renewed per phase/job/process.",
    "phaseDeadline": "min(globalDeadline, t0+absoluteCutoffOffsetMs, actualPhaseStart+capMs). Early finish permits early next phase but never increases local caps.",
    "jobDeadline": "min(phaseDeadline, globalDeadline, slotReservationTime+slotCap); slotReservationTime precedes all job-scoped preflight/setup and is never reset on child spawn. Subphase caps remain inside this absolute slot.",
    "admission": "Reserve the entire declared slot including cleanup before job-scoped work, only if it fits remaining absolute time. Reservation alone admits no child. Initial root validation is inside AUTH setup; phase-start and first-slot reservation share one timestamp. Later child admission inherits the already-consuming slot deadline and must still fit its remaining subphase+cleanup reserves; otherwise UNRUN_BUDGET.",
    "cleanup": "TERM grace1000ms plus known group reap/KILL wait4000ms are inside cleanup allocation, not appended to global cap. No late retry.",
    "supervisor": "Independent owned supervisor enforces absolute deadlines even if worker synchronous hashing/Git/compiler stalls. All admitted work uses known PID/groups; no foreign scan/kill or opaque-host preemption promise.",
    "coordinatorOverhead": "All coordinator bookkeeping, preflight and phase transitions are charged within the current slot setup/guard/evidence allocation; no work is free between phases. Reservations and phase-entry timestamps use the same owner event. These are proposed APIs, not existing clock proof."
  },
